WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:13.160
When you're on the verge of defeat in a duel, what do you need to survive?

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.990
What you need is the inner strength to make your own decisions!

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:23.000
If a duelist doesn't have the courage, he'll lose the match and betray the hopes of his friends!

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:29.700
I still want to protect my friends!  I want to protect Yugi!

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.640
Let's battle!

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.480
Shining Friendship!  Silver Lightning Arrow!

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.150
Harpie Lady is destroyed!

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.250
I lose.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.660
Mai.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.250
Yugi.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.180
Please use these to save your grandpa.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.660
Anzu...

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.400
Okay!  I'll try!

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.920
Yugi!

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:04.000
I'll battle using my own ideas and make my own decisions.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:09.700
That's what it means to be a duelist.  Right, my other self?

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:16.210
Save Mokuba!
Kaiba vs Pegasus

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.140
We finally reached Pegasus's castle.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.130
You guys!

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.000
You collected the Star Chips?

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:32.560
Yeah!

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.740
But only three more participants are allowed to enter the finals.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.120
And we're the three!

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:40.670
What?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.910
We met the requirements.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.840
So there's nothing you can say.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.380
Excuse us.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.720
We finally reached the castle.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.830
Wait!  Where do you think you're going?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.500
We're here for moral support.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.130
What?

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.710
That's not allowed!

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.800
You can't enter the castle!

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.300
How did you even get to this island-

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.940
Don't be so difficult.  Can't you just overlook this?

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.040
For me?  Please?

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.920
No!

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.180
Rules are rules!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.850
I can't ignore-  Hey!

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.520
Push!

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.600
Stop!

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.330
That's what you get!

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.000
You punks!  Open up!

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.970
Okay, let's go.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.770
Just wait, Grandpa.  I'll save you.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.080
That's...

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.240
Bandit Keith!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.920
What a surprise.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.440
You actually made it to the castle?

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.000
Bandit Keith...

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.760
How dare you trap us in that cave!

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.560
Whoa, don't be so upset.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.520
I'll take you on later.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.380
Say what?

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:22.670
An entertaining side show is about to start.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:23.740
Take a look.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.550
That's...

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.130
It's Kaiba.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.760
It's about to start.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.760
A duel between Kaiba and Pegasus.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.580
Kaiba and Pegasus are dueling?

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:42.320
Correct.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:48.600
To the four contestants entering the final championship, welcome to Pegasus's castle.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.540
There seems to be some uninvited guests, but we'll overlook that.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:00.040
You are noble duelists who've won your battles in Duelist Kingdom.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:06.920
Pegasus welcomes you by allowing you to watch his special match.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.100
Sounds like he wants us to witness his skills.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.140
That may be correct.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.540
He's toying with us!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.430
Relax and enjoy the match.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.660
Kaiba...

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.710
Just wait, Mokuba.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:30.100
I promise to defeat Pegasus and save you.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.480
Pegasus!

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:43.760
Welcome to my castle, Kaiba boy.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:51.700
I've been waiting for the day when I could duel such a proud duelist here at Duelist Kingdom.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.820
Don't worry, Kaiba boy.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:01.140
If you beat me in a duel, I will return Mokuba to normal.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:05.740
Kaiba boy, let's have a great duel.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:11.380
Pegasus's Millennium Eye has the power to read his opponent's mind.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:15.910
I actually want both Kaiba and Pegasus to lose.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:22.580
But if Pegasus loses, the championship might be canceled.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:26.780
Yeah.  We have to hope that Kaiba loses.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:32.860
In order to save Grandpa, I know that I must defeat Pegasus.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.020
But for some reason, I don't want Kaiba to lose.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.010
I don't want him to lose.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:44.950
All the participants in the finals have gathered inside my castle.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.150
Kaiba.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.460
Yugi!

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.320
You still managed to enter the castle?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.830
I shouldn't be surprised.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:07:00.800
Yugi boy, it seems that you and I are destined to battle.

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:05.640
Let us begin our duel, Kaiba boy.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:14.440
Pegasus, we'll duel using these Duel Disks.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.590
Am I supposed to wave it like this?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.690
But it's too heavy for that.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:26.290
Or am I supposed to roll it?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:27.830
Stop joking around!

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.640
Then how about this:

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:39.270
I will duel using your Duel Disk, but someone else will throw the Disk in my place.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:40.440
What?

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:47.180
I'll give that person a memo instructing how to play the cards I've selected.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.610
That punk!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:54.750
But we'll still be playing the game as usual.  Understand?

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.820
Pegasus...

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:59.260
Fight me one-on-one!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:04.620
Game strategy dictates that I should never meet my opponent on equal terms.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:09.110
We've already started the psychological part of this game, Kaiba boy.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:15.440
I know your little device can't defeat my Millennium Eye.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:21.380
Bring the person who will throw the Disk in my place.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:27.890
That's...

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.490
Mokuba!

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.590
Mokuba?

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:37.040
It's Mokuba.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.030
He's acting strange.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.260
Pegasus, what did you do to Mokuba?

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.040
What's wrong, Kaiba boy?

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.400
Aren't you happy to be reunited with Mokuba?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.580
Pegasus!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:57.020
Mokuba boy's soul is sealed inside this card.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.690
Sealed inside a card?

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.440
What does he mean?

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.360
Is he hypnotized?

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.580
The Mokuba standing before you has been stripped of his soul.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.940
But he'll still do whatever I tell him.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:23.020
Kaiba boy, if you defeat me, I will release Mokuba boy's soul from this card.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.660
How dare you, Pegasus!

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.120
Mokuba...  No way...

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.400
Pegasus used his dark power to capture Mokuba.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.330
I understand.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:44.760
Kaiba pushed it to the extreme so that he could save Mokuba.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:49.820
Throw the Duel Disk in my place, Mokuba boy.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.500
Wait!

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.440
What's the matter, Kaiba boy?

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:59.110
We're using your Duel Disks to duel, just as you wished.

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:04.320
You expect me to battle against Mokuba?

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:06.590
Big brother!

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.620
Big brother...

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.170
Big brother!

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:18.310
That's the one thing I cannot do.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.400
Kaiba...

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:25.840
Fine, Pegasus.  We won't use Duel Disks.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:32.780
Mokuba boy, your dear brother unfortunately doesn't want to battle against you.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.380
Mokuba...

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.820
Let's prepare for the duel.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:55.370
A Duel Ring is coming down?

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.740
It will finally begin.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:05.420
A duel between Kaiba and Pegasus.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:53.560
We'll play the duel using Kingdom rules.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:58.020
If that's acceptable, set your deck.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:04.140
Kaiba, watch out for Pegasus's Dragon Capture Jar!

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.400
Dragon Capture Jar?

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:12.240
Even your Blue-Eyes White Dragon will be powerless against that Jar.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.680
Choose the cards in your deck carefully, Kaiba.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.850
Yugi, why are you giving advice to Kaiba?

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:24.960
Because Kaiba is battling to save his dear brother Mokuba.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:28.000
He can't afford to lose!

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.660
Yugi...

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:37.280
Yugi, I appreciate your ideas, but I believe in my own cards!

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:44.440
You fool.  He gave good advice.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:52.060
No matter what my opponent's strategy is, I will always battle alongside my Blue-Eyes!

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.490
And I will defeat you!

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.660
Duel!

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:09.000
We'll start with my turn.

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:12.170
I place a monster in defense position.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:18.110
Then I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:22.050
Is it a spell card or a trap card?

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:24.080
My turn!

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.890
I already have one Blue-Eyes in my hand.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.820
I can play it to go on the offensive from the start.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:36.000
But the problem is the Dragon Capture Jar that Yugi mentioned.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.660
I also set one card.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:47.570
Then I play Rude Kaiser in attack position.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.150
Attack the monster in defense position!

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.500
Oh no!

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.220
I end my turn.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:09.260
Kaiba boy's monster has 1800 attack points.

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:13.420
That's 200 points higher than my monster's defense points.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.240
Whoa!  I think I can win with this card!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:22.400
Parrot Dragon, attack!

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:30.080
I'll counter it with a spell card!

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.250
What?

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:34.150
My set card is Mesmeric Control.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:40.160
This card lowers your monster's attack points by 800.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.840
Now, Rude Kaiser!

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.610
Oh no!

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.550
How serious are you, Pegasus?

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:03.400
What's up?  Is Pegasus actually weak?

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.060
He's pathetic.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:06.060
Yeah...

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:09.020
Can it be that Pegasus is...

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:09.880
Yeah.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:13.620
Pegasus always does this.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.830
Don't let your guard down, Kaiba.

00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:22.170
I've provided enough entertainment to liven things up.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:28.460
Kaiba boy, I'm able to read your mind and your hand.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.760
It's my turn!

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:39.220
As the turns pass, there's a higher probability that he has Dragon Capture Jar in his hand.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:47.130
My instincts tell me that he doesn't have Dragon Capture Jar in his hand, so now's my chance!

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:49.860
Stop!

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:52.970
Stop right there.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.950
Make sure that you don't show me your card.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:16:01.070
I activate a trap card that affects the card you're holding in your hand.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:01.880
What?

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:05.440
My set card is Prophecy.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:15.120
I have to guess whether the card in your hand has greater or fewer than 2000 attack points.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.640
If I guess correctly, that card belongs to me.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:20.790
What?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:25.150
I prophesize that it has more than 2000 attack points.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.340
But that's not fun enough.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:32.700
I'll be even more specific.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:40.850
That card is your most trusted card with 3000 attack points: Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:43.980
Impossible.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:48.040
Pegasus knows my hand?

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:57.480
This card now belongs to me.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:04.500
Kaiba boy, how does it feel to have your most trusted card taken from you?

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:07.060
Kaiba lost his Blue-Eyes.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:08.070
Unbelievable.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:13.510
Pegasus must be using the Millennium Eye to read Kaiba's mind.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:18.450
I never knew there was a trap card that lets you take your opponent's card.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:22.690
I add this card to my hand.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.020
Blue-Eyes!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:30.230
Let's continue the duel, Kaiba boy.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:34.870
I switch Rude Kaiser to defense position and end my turn.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:37.300
Then it's my turn.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:40.350
I'll teach you a lesson next turn!

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.910
Your eyes tell me that you're planning something.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:48.950
But it'll be pointless because I can read your thoughts.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.550
Mind Scan!

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:02.400
I see.  You have Crush Card Virus in your hand.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:10.640
You'll use Saggi the Dark Clown as a carrier to activate a virus combo next turn and destroy my deck.

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:15.240
How cunning, but it won't work on me.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:21.680
I set one card and place a monster in defense position.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:24.620
That ends my turn.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.640
It's my turn!

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.840
Pegasus, you're finished this turn!

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.320
My cards form a virus combo!

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:36.960
Saggi the Dark Clown acts as a carrier to activate my Virus!

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:40.960
I'll eradicate your deck!

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:43.270
Go ahead and attack me!

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:45.600
Saggi the Dark Clown.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.710
Is this the virus combo that punished Yugi?

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:51.760
If he pulls it off, Pegasus will be in trouble!

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:52.930
It won't work!

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.380
Pegasus anticipated this!

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.040
What?

00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:00.750
I activate the spell card that I set on the field.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:01.920
What?

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:06.580
And that card is Negative Energy!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:11.700
The attack points of Dark Attribute monsters are doubled!

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:17.740
Saggi the Dark Clown is Dark Attribute, so its attack points are doubled!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:23.180
Oh no!  Crush Card Virus can only use monsters with 1000-or-fewer attack points as carriers!

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:26.610
Your Crush Card Virus is destroyed.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.550
He also anticipated my Crush Card Virus?

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.720
It's my turn.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:37.660
I switch Dark Rabbit to attack position.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:41.300
Since it's Dark Attribute, its attack points are doubled!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:47.200
Dark Rabbit, attack Saggi the Dark Clown.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.620
Oh no!

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:59.440
The virus combo gave Yugi a lot of trouble.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.850
But he easily defeated it!

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.280
Kaiba...

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:18.060
Kaiba boy, fear is beginning to grow within your heart.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.460
But we're only getting started.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:26.660
The world I created will make you feel true terror.

00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:38.800
Pegasus's trump card Toon World finally appears.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.200
When Pegasus's monsters turn into Toons, Kaiba's attacks can't hit them.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:48.290
He turns the Blue-Eyes that he stole into a Toon and pummels Kaiba.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:55.000
Even if you are the creator of Duel Monsters, it's not fair that you're the only one with that card!

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.330
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Kaiba Defeated!
Invincible Toon World

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:00.970
Duel, standby!

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:13.130
The flask glistens

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:20.980
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:29.950
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:37.730
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:43.560
Shower of happiness

00:21:43.850 --> 00:21:47.670
I will shower you with it

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:55.940
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:56.150 --> 00:22:00.180
Shower of happiness

00:22:00.450 --> 00:22:04.310
You are not alone

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:11.030
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
